<title>AUSTRALIA: Westpac aims for 100 bp cost cuts - Joss.</title>
<headline>Westpac aims for 100 bp cost cuts - Joss.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westpac Banking Corp managing director Bob Joss said on Monday that he aimed to cut the bank's costs to about 200 basis points from their current 300 basis point level.</p>
<p>&quot;We have to get somewhere into the neighbourhood of 200 basis points, not the 300 basis points we have now, to run a bank efficiently,&quot; Joss told a Securities Institute luncheon.</p>
<p>He said Westpac needed to continue to reduce its staff and real estate costs and run larger, fewer and more efficient bank branches.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
